%%%
Jointchain-bodied composite kernel under a kernel-broadcast.

Per group g a 3-component positional `jointchain`, so the chain's
per-cell result is [x_0, x_1, x_2]:

  x_0 ~ Normal(m_g, 1)
  x_1 ~ Normal(x_0, 1)
  x_2 ~ Normal(x_0 + x_1, 1)

Step i binds the `cat` of every variate to its left — spec §06 gives
`jointchain(M, K1, K2)` the lowering `a ~ M; b ~ K1(a); c ~ K2([a, b])`.
Step 1 has one variate to its left and binds it whole; step 2 has two
and binds their `cat`, which its body reduces with `sum`. A step that
means the previous state ALONE is `markovchain` instead (see
fixtures/hierarchical-state-space.flatppl).

The executor is `_executeJointChainComposite` (mat-broadcast.ts): the
steps are a scan (sequential, carrying every variate drawn so far), the
cell axis G is parallel and folds into each step's single sampleN.

Closed form (x_1 = x_0 + e_1, x_2 = 2*x_0 + e_1 + e_2, all e ~ N(0,1)):
  E[x_0] = E[x_1] = m_g,  E[x_2] = 2*m_g
  Var = {1, 2, 6},  Cov(x_0, x_2) = 2,  Cov(x_1, x_2) = 3
The cat feed is what those numbers pin: a prev-only step 2 would give
E[x_2] = m_g and Var(x_2) = 3.
%%%
flatppl_compat = "0.1"

m_per_group = [0.0, 1.0, 2.0]

% Step 1: one variate to the left, bound whole.
step_prev = functionof(Normal(mu = _a_, sigma = 1.0), a = _a_)

% Step 2: two variates to the left, bound as their `cat`.
step_cat = functionof(Normal(mu = sum(_b_), sigma = 1.0), b = _b_)

group_chain = functionof(
  jointchain(Normal(mu = _m_, sigma = 1.0), step_prev, step_cat),
  m = _m_)

y = broadcast(group_chain, m = m_per_group)
